    "updated_at": "2024-10-10T12:27:49Z",
    "body": "I also started encountering this recently on my setup (macOS 14.7, iTerm 3.5, zsh 5.9). For me, the solution was \"hidden\" in the issue description. It is broken with this `locale`:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\n$ locale\r\nlocale\r\nLANG=\"\"\r\nLC_COLLATE=\"C\"\r\nLC_CTYPE=\"C\"\r\nLC_MESSAGES=\"C\"\r\nLC_MONETARY=\"C\"\r\nLC_NUMERIC=\"C\"\r\nLC_TIME=\"C\"\r\nLC_ALL=\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut it works if I add this to my `.zshrc`.\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nexport LANG=\"en_US.UTF-8\"\r\nexport LC_ALL=\"en_US.UTF-8\"\r\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
