    "body": "Posting for posterity, on FreeBSD 14.1 RELEASE with:\r\n\r\nzsh 5.9 (amd64-portbld-freebsd14.1)\r\nstarship 1.21.1\r\n\r\nthis suggestion worked for me.\r\n\r\n> I also started encountering this recently on my setup (macOS 14.7, iTerm 3.5, zsh 5.9). For me, the solution was \"hidden\" in the issue description. It is broken with this `locale`:\r\n> \r\n> ```shell\r\n> $ locale\r\n> locale\r\n> LANG=\"\"\r\n> LC_COLLATE=\"C\"\r\n> LC_CTYPE=\"C\"\r\n> LC_MESSAGES=\"C\"\r\n> LC_MONETARY=\"C\"\r\n> LC_NUMERIC=\"C\"\r\n> LC_TIME=\"C\"\r\n> LC_ALL=\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> But it works if I add this to my `.zshrc`.\r\n> \r\n> ```shell\r\n> export LANG=\"en_US.UTF-8\"\r\n> export LC_ALL=\"en_US.UTF-8\"\r\n> ```\r\n\r\n",
